 ## installed and enabled
 
 `extensions.Config(installed, default_enabled)` separates installed extensions from their default selection. multiple compaction strategies may be installed, but at most one can be enabled for a session. built-in sessions start with `rolling`; custom hosts can omit compaction. `runtime.start_with_config(database, config)` uses this selection; `runtime.start_with_extensions(database, installed)` enables every supplied extension.
+
+`daemon/server.main_with_config(config)` runs the complete stock daemon startup
+with a supplied `extensions.Config`. Construct declarations only before calling
+it; installed initialisers run after the home lock is claimed. `main()` retains
+stock defaults. The lower-level `start_with_config(daemon_config, port, config)`
+has the same caller-owned home/authentication/process contract as `start`.
+Executable entrypoints dispatch `storage_cli.arguments()` before constructing a
+custom registry, so offline storage helpers retain their existing ownership.
 
